2026-10-10T04:00:19.6317031Z [org.jetbrains.intellij.platform] Patching plugin.xml: value of 'change-notes[
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6318674Z         <b>0.4.29 / 0.4.30</b> — fix: <b>"Configure LLM" now pre-fills your config</b>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6319870Z         — no more re-typing model+key. The wizard pre-fills your current model, base
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6321002Z         URL and vision model, pre-selects your current provider (✓ 当前), and lets you
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6321999Z         <b>leave the API key blank to keep the stored one</b> (only required when there's
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6323174Z         no key yet or you switch providers). The config itself was never lost — it lives
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6324153Z         in <code>~/.chainlesschain/config.json</code> and survives CLI updates; the
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6325585Z         wizard just didn't pre-fill it. (Mirrors the VS Code 0.34.0 fix. 0.4.30 adds
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6326485Z         this very change-note, which 0.4.29 omitted.)
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6327057Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6328463Z         <b>0.4.28</b> — docs: the Marketplace "What's New" now lists every release
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6329819Z         (it had silently stopped at 0.4.19 — change-notes are no longer missed).
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6330632Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6331505Z         <b>0.4.27</b> — cleared the 2 deprecated-API usages the Marketplace verifier
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6332547Z         flagged (now <code>URI.toURL()</code> + a combo-box dialog), so the plugin
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6333429Z         stays compatible with future IntelliJ releases.
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6334001Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6335087Z         <b>0.4.26</b> — fix: no more false "未检测到 cc CLI" when <code>cc</code> IS
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6336280Z         installed. The version probe timeout went 5s → 12s (cold starts), and since
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6337388Z         <code>cc</code> is also the C compiler's name, the plugin now resolves the
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6338756Z         binary with fallback (<code>cc → chainlesschain → clc → clchain</code>) and
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6339685Z         uses it for the chat spawn and every probe.
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6340284Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6341042Z         <b>0.4.25</b> — the agent can actually ask you a question:
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6342073Z         <code>ask_user_question</code> now pops a dialog (single-choice / multi-select
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6343229Z         checkboxes / free-text input) so the agent can clarify instead of guessing.
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6344232Z         Requires <code>cc</code> ≥ 0.162.95.
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6395158Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6396115Z         <b>0.4.24</b> — fix: a graceful "couldn't ask in the panel" degradation no
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6397172Z         longer renders as a scary <b>✗ ask_user_question</b> failure.
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6397802Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6398563Z         <b>0.4.23</b> — new <b>⚙ LLM → 检查 cc 更新…</b> menu item (check on demand),
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6399454Z         plus a clear hint when the <code>cc</code> CLI isn't installed.
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6400074Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6400852Z         <b>0.4.22</b> — you're now told when a newer <code>cc</code> CLI is published
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6401681Z         on npm, so you don't silently miss new features.
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6402329Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6403117Z         <b>0.4.21</b> — fix: reconfiguring the LLM now restarts the running chat so it
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6404190Z         picks up the new provider/model/key (no more "配置完还没用 / 新开对话才行").
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6405040Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6405811Z         <b>0.4.20</b> — new <code>/review</code> command: review your uncommitted git
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6407007Z         diff right from the chat (matches the VS Code panel).
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6407597Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6408322Z         <b>0.4.19</b> — fix: the suggested vision model now matches the CLI's
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6409275Z         actual default (<code>doubao-seed-2-0-lite-260215</code>) instead of an
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6410144Z         older snapshot, so the prefilled value equals what
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6410792Z         <code>cc agent --image</code> uses.
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6411275Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6412002Z         <b>0.4.18</b> — dedicated image-recognition (vision) model entry: the
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6413079Z         <b>⚙ LLM</b> button is now a small menu (configure full LLM <i>or</i> just
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6414138Z         the vision model), plus a <b>Tools → Configure Vision Model</b> action.
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6415339Z         Set <code>llm.visionModel</code> without re-running the whole wizard or
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6416251Z         re-typing your API key; blank reverts to the text model.
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6416835Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6417584Z         <b>0.4.17</b> — first-run nudge: when no LLM provider is configured yet,
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6418887Z         the chat panel now shows a dim hint pointing at the <b>⚙ LLM</b> button
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6419889Z         instead of staying blank until the first turn fails with a 401 (VS Code
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6445328Z         onboarding parity).
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6445786Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6446607Z         <b>0.4.16</b> — chat panel LLM UX: (1) paste screenshots — Ctrl/Cmd+V an
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6447656Z         image to attach it to your next message (vision); (2) a <b>⚙ LLM</b>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6448604Z         quick-entry button by Send opens the provider/model wizard, and auth
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6449564Z         failures (401/403/missing key) now hint at it; (3) the wizard can set a
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6450710Z         separate <b>image-recognition (vision) model</b> — text and vision models
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6451479Z         no longer have to be the same.
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6451955Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6452670Z         <b>0.4.15</b> — multi-line chat composer: the input now wraps across
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6453670Z         lines — <b>Enter</b> sends, <b>Shift+Enter</b> adds a newline (VS Code
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6454315Z         parity).
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6454859Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6455656Z         <b>0.4.14</b> — extended-thinking reasoning (with <code>/think</code>) now
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6456576Z         streams into the transcript dimmed/italic, set apart from the answer
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6457247Z         (VS Code parity).
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6457635Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6458370Z         <b>0.4.13</b> — Markdown rendering in the chat transcript: fenced/inline
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6459294Z         <code>code</code> (monospace) and <b>bold</b> now render instead of raw
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6460250Z         markers (VS Code parity). Streaming stays plain, then snaps to styled.
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6460918Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6461637Z         <b>0.4.12</b> — "Fix with ChainlessChain" intention: on an error/warning
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6462625Z         line, Alt+Enter offers a quick-fix that seeds the chat with a fix request
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6463490Z         scoped to that file + those problems (VS Code parity).
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6464054Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6464987Z         <b>0.4.11</b> — slash-command autocomplete: typing <code>/</code> at the
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6465865Z         start of the chat input pops a chooser of the panel's commands
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6466855Z         (<code>/new</code>, <code>/compact</code>, <code>/think</code>, …),
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6467566Z         filtered as you type (VS Code parity).
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6468079Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6468996Z         <b>0.4.10</b> — fix: wrap the diff-review document reads
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6469867Z         (<code>openDiff</code>/<code>openMultiDiff</code>) in a read action.
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6470780Z         Since 2026.2 the EDT no longer grants implicit read access, so building
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6471692Z         the diff threw "Read access is allowed from inside read-action only" on
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6472440Z         2026.2+. No behavior change on 2025.x.
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6472920Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6473633Z         <b>0.4.9</b> — fix: the chat tool window now deterministically uses the
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6474545Z         LLM provider you configured (<code>cc config</code> / Configure LLM),
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6536310Z         reading <code>~/.chainlesschain/config.json</code> and passing it
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6537412Z         explicitly to <code>cc agent</code> — no more spurious
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6538423Z         <code>Anthropic error: 401</code> when another provider is configured.
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6539161Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6539927Z         <b>0.4.8</b> — <code>/compact</code> in the chat tool window (Claude-Code
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6540896Z         IDE parity): trims the live conversation history between turns (no extra
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6542132Z         LLM call) and reports the tokens saved. Mirrors the VS Code 0.31.0
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6542794Z         feature.
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6543139Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6543919Z         <b>0.4.7</b> — cleared the remaining API-compatibility flags the Plugin
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6545111Z         Verifier reported on 2026.x: the @-mention list renderer no longer uses a
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6546121Z         scheduled-for-removal helper, and the deprecated terminal customizer was
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6547126Z         removed (a <code>cc</code> you run in a terminal still auto-connects via the
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6547897Z         bridge's discovery lockfile).
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6548383Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6549124Z         <b>0.4.6</b> — newer-IDE compatibility: removed the last deprecated-API
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6550122Z         usages (terminal-process listener + provider-chooser dialog). Plugin Verifier
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6551210Z         reports no internal / scheduled-for-removal / deprecated API usage on 2025.2.
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6551965Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6552769Z         <b>0.4.5</b> — reverted the experimental 0.4.4 <code>getTerminalOutput</code>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6553778Z         tool: the terminal API it used is not stable across IDE versions and caused
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6554918Z         errors on some builds. Everything else is unchanged from 0.4.3.
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6555568Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6556302Z         <b>0.4.3</b> — the <code>@</code>-mention symbol completion now covers
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6557334Z         <b>methods/functions</b> too (not just classes) — type a method name to
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6558114Z         reference the file where it's defined.
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6558585Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6559324Z         <b>0.4.2</b> — the <code>@</code>-mention popup now includes project class
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6560263Z         symbols (type a class name to reference the file where it's defined),
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6561226Z         alongside <code>@selection</code>/<code>@diagnostics</code> and files.
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6561906Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6562740Z         <b>0.4.1</b> — expanded the plugin description / what's-new (no functional
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6563441Z         change since 0.4.0).
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6563868Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6564419Z         <b>0.4.0</b> — VS Code feature parity.
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6593163Z         <ul>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6593978Z           <li>Multi-conversation <b>tabs</b> (one agent per tab, resume across restarts).</li>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6595564Z           <li><b>Approval modes</b> (<code>/auto</code>·<code>/bypass</code>·<code>/normal</code>)
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6597170Z               and <b>extended thinking</b> (<code>/think</code>·<code>/ultrathink</code>·<code>/think-off</code>),
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6598410Z               plus <code>/new</code> <code>/stop</code> <code>/cost</code> <code>/context</code>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6599466Z               <code>/plan</code> <code>/approve</code> <code>/reject</code>.</li>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6600769Z           <li><b>Interactive plan &amp; approval cards</b> (Approve/Deny buttons).</li>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6601932Z           <li>Editor <b>Explain / Refactor</b> actions, <code>@file#L</code> reference
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6603066Z               insertion (<code>Ctrl/Cmd+Alt+K</code>), and an <code>@</code>-mention popup.</li>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6604510Z           <li>Native diff "<b>Request changes…</b>" with inline notes, and batch
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6605599Z               <b>openMultiDiff</b> multi-file review.</li>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6606388Z           <li><b>In-editor app preview</b> (JCEF) with Start/Stop.</li>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6607361Z           <li>Live context-window indicator; new-chat / reopen-closed shortcuts.</li>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6608093Z         </ul>
2026-10-10T04:00:19.6627980Z     ]' tag will be set to '<b>[0.4.158] - Pair with CLI model review and diagnostic evidence (2026-10-09)</b><br/><ul><li>Recommend CLI <code>0.166.96</code> after its public npm release and this extension's exact-commit release gates pass.</li><li>Keep Doctor and upgrade prompts aligned with the paired CLI recommendation.</li><li>Retain the compatibility floor and runtime capability diagnostics; experimental native review and durable Windows/macOS recovery remain outside release acceptance.</li></ul><br/><b>[0.4.157] - Pair with strict settings write fairness (2026-10-08)</b><br/><ul><li>Recommend CLI <code>0.166.94</code> after its public npm release and this plugin's exact-commit release gates pass.</li><li>Keep Doctor and the upgrade prompt on the same current CLI recommendation, including artifacts produced by incremental builds.</li><li>Refresh the compiled recommendation and upgrade guidance for concurrent permission-rule writes while retaining the compatibility floor and live capability diagnostics.</li></ul><br/><b>[0.4.156] - Pair with bounded investigation recovery (2026-10-08)</b><br/><ul><li>Recommend CLI <code>0.166.93</code>, Session Core <code>0.3.18</code>, and Context Memory Kernel <code>0.1.8</code> after their public npm release and the plugin's exact-commit release gates pass.</li><li>Refresh the compiled CLI upgrade recommendation and paired release guidance for bounded evidence investigations and organization goal services.</li><li>Repair the dependency setup used to aggregate three-platform accessibility and performance evidence without changing producer requirements.</li></ul><br/><b>[0.4.155] - Candidate runtime and restart validation fixes (2026-10-07)</b><br/><ul><li>Recommend CLI <code>0.166.92</code> after its public npm release and the plugin's exact-commit release gates pass; this entry does not establish publication.</li><li>Pair with Session Core <code>0.3.17</code> and Context/Memory Kernel <code>0.1.7<